# VS-13 S1.1 follow-up (2026-05-04, addresses PR #73 + PR #74 reviews):
#
# `engines.node: ">=22.13.0"` in package.json is ADVISORY by default —
# npm prints a warning but still installs on Node < 22.13. PR #73 review
# flagged that the >=22.0.0 advisory didn't actually enforce. PR #74
# review noted the dep tree's strictest requirement is jsdom 29's
# `^22.13.0` (vite 8 / rolldown declare `>=22.12.0`, jsdom is the
# binding constraint). `engines.node` is now pinned at `>=22.13.0`.
#
# `engine-strict=true` makes `npm install` fail outright when the
# running Node doesn't match `engines`. Combined with CI's
# `actions/setup-node@v4` pinning Node 22.x LTS, this turns the floor
# from advisory into hard enforcement at both install-time and CI-time.
#
# Local devs hitting this on Node < 22.13 should `nvm use 22` (latest
# 22.x LTS is on 22.20+ as of 2026-05). Error points to engines field.
engine-strict=true
